    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your heart is a strong muscle, about the size of your fist. It sits inside your chest.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "✊",
        "text": "As big as your fist",
        "cue": "fist",
        "sub": "Inside your chest",
        "sub_cue": "chest"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "But how can a muscle push blood?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It squeezes, then relaxes, over and over. Each squeeze pushes blood out through tubes called blood vessels.",
      "punch": "squeezes",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Squeeze and relax",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Squeeze!",
            "icon": "💪",
            "cue": "squeezes"
          },
          {
            "label": "Relax and fill up",
            "icon": "😌",
            "cue": "relaxes"
          },
          {
            "label": "Blood rushes down tubes",
            "icon": "🩸",
            "cue": "vessels"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Where does all that blood go?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "One side of your heart sends blood to your lungs, to pick up oxygen from the air you breathe.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/healthy-lung",
        "text": "Off to the lungs!",
        "cue": "lungs",
        "sub": "Pick up oxygen",
        "sub_cue": "oxygen"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "The other side pumps that fresh blood all around your body, to your head, your arms and your toes.",
      "board": {
        "type": "body",
        "title": "Blood's big trip",
        "show": [
          "heart",
          "lungs"
        ],
        "flow": "blood",
        "cue": "blood",
        "labels": [
          {
            "text": "Heart",
            "at": "heart",
            "cue": "pumps"
          },
          {
            "text": "Head",
            "at": "head",
            "cue": "head"
          },
          {
            "text": "Arms",
            "at": "arm",
            "cue": "arms"
          },
          {
            "text": "Toes",
            "at": "foot",
            "cue": "toes"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What's that thump-thump sound I can hear?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "That lub-dub is your heart's little doors, called valves, closing to keep blood going the right way.",
      "punch": "valves",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/heart-valves",
        "text": "Heart valves",
        "cue": "valves",
        "sub": "Lub-dub, lub-dub!",
        "sub_cue": "lub"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why does it beat faster when I run?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Busy muscles need more oxygen, so your heart speeds up. Running and playing keep your heart strong!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💓",
        "text": "Your heart speeds up",
        "cue": "speeds",
        "sub": "Play keeps it strong",
        "sub_cue": "playing"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So my heart squeezes, sends blood to my lungs, then all around me!",
